{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The YubiKit Swift SDK provides a modern async\/await version of the YubiKit framework, making it easy to integrate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in Swift and SwiftUI based applications. The async\/await syntax provides an easy to read and powerful way of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"creating connections and sending commands to the different applications on the YubiKey.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()"]},{"name":"Warning","type":"aside","style":"warning","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This SDK does not perform zeroization of sensitive data in memory. Cryptographic keys, PIN tokens,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and other secrets are not securely erased when no longer in use. This is currently out of scope but may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"addressed in a future release.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yubikit"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Connect and run commands on the different applications on a YubiKey. The framework support connecting using NFC, Lightning and USB.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Preparing your project","identifiers":["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Preparing-your-project"},{"title":"Sample code","identifiers":["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/OATHSampleCode","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/PIVToolSampleCode","doc:\/\/yubikit-s